WEBVTT

NOTE
Generated from prototype/narration.md. Edit that file, not this one.

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Landscape answers one question: who else is already doing what you are planning to do?

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:08.500
You describe your idea in the box, in your own words. That is the only thing you have to do.

3
00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:12.000
Here the idea is an app that helps small farms sell straight to local restaurants.

4
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.500
First it works out what to call this line of business, then goes looking for companies already in it.

5
00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:19.500
It reads each company own website. One site would not let a program read it, so that page is listed with a link, for you to open yourself.

6
00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:23.500
It found three companies you may never have heard of. That is the point: you do not have to know the names in advance.

7
00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:28.500
Prices come first. They are taken straight from each company own price page, so the figures are exactly what they published.

8
00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:32.500
One company does not publish a price at all, so the report says that instead of guessing.

9
00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:36.500
Somebody blog gives a price for the third company. It is not the company own figure, so it stays out of the table, but it is reported underneath with a link and a note saying why we could not confirm it.

10
00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:41.500
Then the written part appears, a few words at a time.

11
00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:46.500
The table of what each one does is careful. A question mark means we looked and found nothing said either way.

12
00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:50.500
And a triangle means a rival claimed it, not the company itself.

13
00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:55.500
When a company does not say what it has changed, the report says exactly that, and lists everywhere it looked.

14
00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:58.500
Customer reviews are read for what people wish the product did. Six people wanted a different price list for each restaurant. That is a gap you could build into.

15
00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:03.500
It also looks up how busy each website is, and when each company started, from services the companies do not control.

16
00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:08.500
Each line says which service it came from and when. These are rankings against every other website, not visitor counts, because visitor numbers are guesses.

17
00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:14.500
Every fact links back to where it came from. Click one and you see the page, the exact sentence, and when it was read.
